# EcoLoop MQTT ACL — least privilege.
#
# backend: full control of the station tree (issues commands, consumes
#          telemetry/events for ALL stations).
# station: may ONLY consume its own command topics and publish its own
#          telemetry/event topics. No cross-station access, no wildcards
#          beyond its own $STATION_CODE prefix, no $SYS read.
#
# The mobile app NEVER receives broker credentials and never connects to
# MQTT — it talks to the backend API/WebSocket only.

user backend
topic readwrite ecoloop/stations/#

# Per-station identity pattern (repeat per physical station, substituting
# the station code). Example for ST-001:
#
# user station-ST-001
# topic read ecoloop/stations/ST-001/command
# topic read ecoloop/stations/ST-001/capture_request
# topic write ecoloop/stations/ST-001/state
# topic write ecoloop/stations/ST-001/sensor
# topic write ecoloop/stations/ST-001/event
# topic write ecoloop/stations/ST-001/heartbeat
